WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.350 --> 00:00:02.142
Joining Ideas and Opinions.

2
00:00:02.422 --> 00:00:05.985
Day 10 of the Soft Skill Playbook course, in the English phase.

3
00:00:07.735 --> 00:00:08.759
The key idea.

4
00:00:09.039 --> 00:00:17.209
Today's goal: join short sentences into longer, natural ones, give reasons, and share, agree with or disagree with an opinion.

5
00:00:18.559 --> 00:00:19.413
Part 1.

6
00:00:19.693 --> 00:00:20.759
Linking words.

7
00:00:22.009 --> 00:00:23.375
Here is a quick table:

8
00:00:23.655 --> 00:00:25.937
Word, and Job, and Example. and.

9
00:00:26.217 --> 00:00:27.369
Job: add.

10
00:00:27.649 --> 00:00:28.524
Example:

11
00:00:28.804 --> 00:00:31.321
I booked the tickets and paid online. but.

12
00:00:31.601 --> 00:00:32.860
Job: contrast.

13
00:00:33.140 --> 00:00:34.015
Example:

14
00:00:34.295 --> 00:00:37.495
The hotel was nice, but the food was average. because.

15
00:00:37.775 --> 00:00:39.012
Job: reason.

16
00:00:39.292 --> 00:00:40.167
Example:

17
00:00:40.447 --> 00:00:42.943
I was late because the metro stopped. so.

18
00:00:43.223 --> 00:00:44.460
Job: result.

19
00:00:44.740 --> 00:00:45.615
Example:

20
00:00:45.895 --> 00:00:48.199
The metro stopped, so I was late. or.

21
00:00:48.479 --> 00:00:49.567
Job: choice.

22
00:00:49.847 --> 00:00:50.721
Example:

23
00:00:51.001 --> 00:00:53.028
We can take a cab or walk. if.

24
00:00:53.308 --> 00:00:54.588
Job: condition.

25
00:00:54.868 --> 00:00:55.743
Example:

26
00:00:56.023 --> 00:00:58.177
If it rains, we'll stay home. when.

27
00:00:58.457 --> 00:00:59.460
Job: time.

28
00:00:59.740 --> 00:01:00.615
Example:

29
00:01:00.895 --> 00:01:04.265
When I reach the station, I'll call you. although or even though.

30
00:01:04.545 --> 00:01:06.359
Job: surprising contrast.

31
00:01:06.639 --> 00:01:07.513
Example:

32
00:01:07.793 --> 00:01:10.055
Although it was expensive, it was worth it.

33
00:01:11.405 --> 00:01:12.493
also or too.

34
00:01:12.773 --> 00:01:13.925
Job: add.

35
00:01:14.205 --> 00:01:15.079
Example:

36
00:01:15.359 --> 00:01:18.901
I also need a receipt. / I need a receipt too. however.

37
00:01:19.181 --> 00:01:21.549
Job: contrast (formal, new sentence).

38
00:01:21.829 --> 00:01:22.703
Example:

39
00:01:22.983 --> 00:01:24.135
The plan is good.

40
00:01:24.415 --> 00:01:26.570
However, it's risky. for example.

41
00:01:26.850 --> 00:01:28.109
Job: example.

42
00:01:28.389 --> 00:01:29.263
Example:

43
00:01:29.543 --> 00:01:32.637
We need better tests, for example for the payment flow.

44
00:01:33.987 --> 00:01:34.733
Warning:

45
00:01:35.013 --> 00:01:36.016
Don't double up.

46
00:01:36.296 --> 00:01:41.779
Although it was late, but I went. then Although it was late, I went. or It was late, but I went.

47
00:01:42.059 --> 00:01:45.877
Because I was sick, so I didn't come. then Because I was sick, I didn't come.

48
00:01:47.227 --> 00:01:49.489
Part 2. if sentences (conditions).

49
00:01:50.739 --> 00:01:52.104
Here is a quick table:

50
00:01:52.384 --> 00:01:54.261
Type, and Pattern, and Example.

51
00:01:54.541 --> 00:01:55.757
Real or likely.

52
00:01:56.037 --> 00:01:56.869
Pattern:

53
00:01:57.149 --> 00:01:59.005
If + present, will + verb.

54
00:01:59.285 --> 00:02:00.160
Example:

55
00:02:00.440 --> 00:02:02.552
If the train is late, I'll take a cab.

56
00:02:02.832 --> 00:02:03.813
Always true.

57
00:02:04.093 --> 00:02:04.925
Pattern:

58
00:02:05.205 --> 00:02:06.720
If + present, present.

59
00:02:07.000 --> 00:02:07.875
Example:

60
00:02:08.155 --> 00:02:10.203
If you press this, the light turns on.

61
00:02:10.483 --> 00:02:11.464
Imaginary.

62
00:02:11.744 --> 00:02:12.576
Pattern:

63
00:02:12.856 --> 00:02:14.669
If + past, would + verb.

64
00:02:14.949 --> 00:02:15.824
Example:

65
00:02:16.104 --> 00:02:18.280
If I had more time, I would learn French.

66
00:02:19.630 --> 00:02:20.526
Part 3.

67
00:02:20.806 --> 00:02:21.958
Giving opinions.

68
00:02:23.208 --> 00:02:24.573
Here is a quick table:

69
00:02:24.853 --> 00:02:27.563
Opinion, and Agree, and Disagree (politely).

70
00:02:27.843 --> 00:02:28.696
I think...

71
00:02:28.976 --> 00:02:29.787
Agree:

72
00:02:30.067 --> 00:02:32.840
I agree. / Exactly! / That's true.

73
00:02:33.120 --> 00:02:34.528
Disagree (politely):

74
00:02:34.808 --> 00:02:36.152
I'm not sure about that.

75
00:02:36.432 --> 00:02:37.584
In my opinion...

76
00:02:37.864 --> 00:02:38.675
Agree:

77
00:02:38.955 --> 00:02:40.277
I feel the same way.

78
00:02:40.557 --> 00:02:41.965
Disagree (politely):

79
00:02:42.245 --> 00:02:43.717
I see it a bit differently.

80
00:02:43.997 --> 00:02:45.043
I feel that...

81
00:02:45.323 --> 00:02:46.133
Agree:

82
00:02:46.413 --> 00:02:47.267
You're right.

83
00:02:47.547 --> 00:02:48.955
Disagree (politely):

84
00:02:49.235 --> 00:02:50.664
That's a good point, but...

85
00:02:50.944 --> 00:02:52.011
If you ask me...

86
00:02:52.291 --> 00:02:53.101
Agree:

87
00:02:53.381 --> 00:02:54.384
Absolutely.

88
00:02:54.664 --> 00:02:56.072
Disagree (politely):

89
00:02:56.352 --> 00:02:57.973
I agree up to a point, but...

90
00:02:58.253 --> 00:02:59.107
I'd say...

91
00:02:59.387 --> 00:03:00.197
Agree:

92
00:03:00.477 --> 00:03:01.352
Good point.

93
00:03:01.632 --> 00:03:03.040
Disagree (politely):

94
00:03:03.320 --> 00:03:05.176
I'm afraid I don't agree, because...

95
00:03:06.526 --> 00:03:07.486
Give a reason:

96
00:03:07.766 --> 00:03:12.395
I think we should take the train, because it's faster than the bus and we can work on the way.

97
00:03:13.745 --> 00:03:14.663
Part 4.

98
00:03:14.943 --> 00:03:17.119
Conversation: deciding where to eat.

99
00:03:18.369 --> 00:03:20.395
Here is how the conversation goes.

100
00:03:20.675 --> 00:03:22.467
Where should we go for the team lunch?

101
00:03:22.747 --> 00:03:27.569
I think we should try the new Andhra place, because everyone likes spicy food.

102
00:03:27.849 --> 00:03:29.662
That's true, but it's a bit far.

103
00:03:29.942 --> 00:03:31.819
It takes twenty minutes to get there.

104
00:03:32.099 --> 00:03:33.038
Good point.

105
00:03:33.318 --> 00:03:36.390
If we leave at 12:30, we'll be back by 2.

106
00:03:36.670 --> 00:03:39.230
Although it's far, the food is really good.

107
00:03:40.580 --> 00:03:42.180
The conversation continues.

108
00:03:42.460 --> 00:03:43.079
Hmm.

109
00:03:43.359 --> 00:03:45.065
What about the vegetarians?

110
00:03:45.345 --> 00:03:49.100
They have a big vegetarian menu too, so it should be fine.

111
00:03:49.380 --> 00:03:50.681
Okay, I agree.

112
00:03:50.961 --> 00:03:52.647
Let's book a table for ten.

113
00:03:52.927 --> 00:03:53.673
Great.

114
00:03:53.953 --> 00:03:55.767
I'll call them now and book it.

115
00:03:57.117 --> 00:03:58.077
Part 5.

116
00:03:58.357 --> 00:03:59.274
Practice.

117
00:04:00.524 --> 00:04:01.164
1.

118
00:04:01.444 --> 00:04:03.215
Join with and, but, because, so.

119
00:04:03.495 --> 00:04:04.497
It was raining.

120
00:04:04.777 --> 00:04:05.993
I took an umbrella.

121
00:04:06.273 --> 00:04:06.977
2.

122
00:04:07.257 --> 00:04:08.452
I like my job.

123
00:04:08.732 --> 00:04:09.991
It's very stressful.

124
00:04:10.271 --> 00:04:11.017
3.

125
00:04:11.297 --> 00:04:12.300
I was tired.

126
00:04:12.580 --> 00:04:13.839
I went to bed early.

127
00:04:15.189 --> 00:04:16.106
Success:

128
00:04:16.386 --> 00:04:17.239
Answers.

129
00:04:17.519 --> 00:04:19.610
It was raining, so I took an umbrella.

130
00:04:19.890 --> 00:04:20.594
2.

131
00:04:20.874 --> 00:04:23.242
I like my job, but it's very stressful.

132
00:04:23.522 --> 00:04:25.783
I went to bed early because I was tired.

133
00:04:26.063 --> 00:04:26.725
(or:

134
00:04:27.005 --> 00:04:29.245
I was tired, so I went to bed early.).

135
00:04:30.595 --> 00:04:31.299
2.

136
00:04:31.579 --> 00:04:32.432
Complete.

137
00:04:32.712 --> 00:04:35.613
If the flight is cancelled,. / If I had a car,.

138
00:04:36.963 --> 00:04:37.881
Success:

139
00:04:38.161 --> 00:04:42.427
Sample answers. ...I'll book a train ticket. /...I would drive to work.

140
00:04:43.777 --> 00:04:44.524
3.

141
00:04:44.804 --> 00:04:46.447
Give your opinion with a reason:

142
00:04:46.727 --> 00:04:49.607
Is working from home better than working in the office?

143
00:04:50.957 --> 00:04:51.895
Part 6.

144
00:04:52.175 --> 00:04:53.221
Speak today.

145
00:04:54.471 --> 00:04:57.564
Use because and so in at least 3 sentences each.

146
00:04:57.844 --> 00:05:00.703
Give one opinion at work with I think... because...

147
00:05:00.983 --> 00:05:02.519
Disagree once politely:

148
00:05:02.799 --> 00:05:04.313
I see it a bit differently...

149
00:05:05.663 --> 00:05:07.199
That's the end of this lesson.

150
00:05:07.479 --> 00:05:12.151
Pick one script from it, say it out loud three times, and use it for real today.

151
00:05:12.431 --> 00:05:18.533
For extra practice, paste the Master Prompt into an AI assistant and role-play the conversation.

